<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Monochrome notification icon (spec §6.4). Android 8+ ("Miscellaneous"
  channel fallback aside) renders every notification's small icon as a solid
  white silhouette on the status bar regardless of the source colors, so this
  must be alpha-only art - any RGB here is discarded, only the alpha channel
  shapes the silhouette. Without this, FCM/the OS falls back to the launcher
  icon, which gets forced into a solid white blob with no recognizable shape.

  Bell glyph (matches the in-app Notifications section icon, `i-bell` /
  Phosphor BellIcon, "fill" weight) traced at its native 256x256 viewBox.
-->
